meta {
  name: Create custom product (TICKET-P6-007)
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/custom-products
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Negroni",
    "imageKey": "{{productImageKey}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setEnvVar("productId", res.getBody().id);
  }
}

docs {
  TICKET-P6-007 — create a barcode-less custom product (a cocktail, a dish, loose-leaf tea —
  anything with no GTIN). Registered users only; anonymous tokens 403.

  Body: { name, imageKey? }.
  - `name` — required, 1–80 characters after trimming (the 80 cap is measured on the raw,
    untrimmed string).
  - `imageKey` — optional. A server-issued `processed/{uuid}.jpg` key from
    Upload image with `kind: item` (NOT `kind: product` — that prompt expects packaging).

  Any packaged-only field (gtin/barcode, brand, genericName, energyKcal, carbohydrates, sugars,
  fat, saturatedFat, protein, salt, servingSize, ingredients, allergens) in the body is a 400 —
  a custom product's identity is its name alone (ADR 0006) and it structurally cannot hold
  nutrition/allergen data, so the server never silently drops these, it rejects the request.

  Creates a `Product` row with kind: CUSTOM, status: PENDING_REVIEW, no PackagedProduct row.
  Same lifecycle as a user-submitted packaged product from here: peer review via
  Approve/Reject product, anyone can rate it immediately (incl. anonymously and the creator),
  and renames go through Correct product / Propose product edit.

  Duplicate names: the server normalises the name (Unicode NFKD, diacritics stripped,
  lowercased, whitespace collapsed+trimmed) and enforces uniqueness among non-REJECTED CUSTOM
  products at the database layer — "Negroni", "negroni" and "Négroni " collide. A REJECTED
  custom product never blocks its name being reused.

  Response:
  - 201 { id, status: 'PENDING_REVIEW' }. The post-response script stores `id` as `productId`
    for the chained verify/correct/edit/rate requests.
  - 400 { message } — validation failure (missing/over-long name, or a packaged-only field).
  - 403 — anonymous session ({ error: 'Registration required' }).
  - 409 { code: 'duplicate_name', productId, message } — another non-REJECTED custom product
    already has this (normalised) name; `productId` is that existing row. The client should
    navigate there instead of retrying.
}
